the multiple-testing arithmetic of a data-quality suite:
 checks k   alpha   P(>=1 false alarm)  clean days per alarm
        5    0.01                4.9%                  20.4
       20    0.01               18.2%                   5.5
      100    0.01               63.4%                   1.6
      400    0.01               98.2%                   1.0

With 400 checks at a 1% per-check false-positive rate you get an alert on
98% of perfectly good days. A suite nobody believes is worse than no suite:
size the thresholds so the aggregate false-alarm rate is what you can staff.
