===== w9c3.py =====
no index:
    SCAN m
    SEARCH t USING AUTOMATIC COVERING INDEX (sym=?)
    result 6,762 rows; nested-loop comparisons if scanned: 20,000 x 2,000 = 40,000,000

with an index on master(sym):
    SCAN t
    BLOOM FILTER ON m (sym=?)
    SEARCH m USING INDEX ix_master_sym (sym=?)
    result 6,762 rows (identical: True); B-tree probes: 20,000 x ceil(log2 2,000) = 220,000
    work ratio: 182x fewer comparisons

with a covering index on master(sector, sym):
    SCAN t
    SEARCH m USING COVERING INDEX ix_master_sector_sym (sector=? AND sym=?)
    result 6,762 rows

note the first plan: with no index available sqlite BUILT one on the fly
(AUTOMATIC COVERING INDEX) -- it paid the build cost inside the query,
every time you run it, instead of once at schema time.

read the plan, not the clock. SCAN means every row; SEARCH ... USING INDEX
means a B-tree probe per outer row. The asymptotics are n*m versus n*log m,
and that gap is why an unindexed research join dies as the panel grows.
